{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"Independent review of PR #424 found that a stale or recycled process-group ID could receive signals, the exit poll spun on EPERM, and the regression did not prove the exact leader-dead retirement path.","decision":"Probe process-group signalability before each group signal and skip it for ESRCH/EPERM; stop polling promptly on EPERM; use nonblocking waitpid on the owned Process so Linux Foundation stale isRunning state is resolved and reaped; strengthen the fixture test to assert leader-dead state, group membership before shutdown, and group removal after shutdown.","impact":"Changed only ACP process lifecycle and ACP backend tests. No Core or public contract changes. Red evidence: focused test failed with the early-return retirement path because the descendant and group survived. Green evidence: focused test passed with group cleanup. `make verify`, `make acp-smoke`, `make runner-smoke`, and `git diff --check` passed.","recurrence_control":"The regression reads the same backend process-state helper used by stopProcess before shutdown; group signals require a successful pre-probe; the bounded group wait treats EPERM as non-waitable instead of spinning.","rejected_alternatives":[],"sources":[]}
